    "methods_description": "EEG data were acquired from 20 healthy subjects at a sampling rate of 256 Hz using 16 channels arranged in a standard 10-20 montage. Recordings were obtained using g.USBamp hardware (g.tec) with a 60 Hz line frequency. Subjects performed a visual P300 speller task using a 9x8 checkerboard paradigm with dynamic stimulus presentation. Each subject completed one session with target and non-target visual stimuli presented in a calibration-then-test cross-validation design.",
